# GitHub feature workflow (Jarvis)

Default delivery path: **feature branch → PR → `main`**. Every feature branch has a matching GitHub issue. All issue/PR/branch text is **English**.

## Naming

```
feature/<issue-number>-<slug-from-issue-title>
```

- `<issue-number>` = GitHub issue number (e.g. `8`)
- `<slug-from-issue-title>` = issue title adapted to a short kebab-case slug (lowercase, hyphens, no punctuation)

Examples: issue `#8` “Fix session history and ChatState vs checkpoints” → `feature/8-fix-session-history-and-chatstate`.

## When on `main` and the user asks for a **new** change

**Propose** (do not start until they confirm) this flow:

1. Create a GitHub issue for the work
2. Create the associated feature branch from up-to-date `main`
3. Develop on that branch

Then follow [`.cursor/skills/github-feature-flow/SKILL.md`](../skills/github-feature-flow/SKILL.md).

## When on `main` and the user asks to solve / work on issue `#X`

Do **not** create a new issue. Proceed (no need to re-propose the full flow):

1. Read the issue with `gh issue view X` (title, body, checklist).
2. Check out the existing development branch for `#X`, or create it if missing (`feature/X-<slug>` from up-to-date `main`).
3. Develop there against the issue requirements; expand the issue body when useful.

Details: same skill file, section “Work on an existing issue”.

## Already on a feature branch

- Implement the requested changes on the current branch.
- When new scope genuinely belongs on the same issue, **expand the issue body** (English) without asking — only when it adds clear value; do not spam trivial edits.

## Pull requests

- Create a PR only when the user asks.
- Title ends with a space and `(#X)` where `X` is the issue number, e.g. `Fix session history after restart (#8)`.
- Link the PR to the issue as development work (`Closes #X` or Development sidebar / `gh` linking). Body in English.

## Out of scope here

Commit message format stays Conventional Commits (see global incremental-commits rules). Do not push or open PRs unless the user requests it.
